Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `owned` was consumed by a lambda that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/task_capture_moved_in_body_then_used_after.jet:20:17
    |
 20 |     print(owned.name)
    |                 ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/task_capture_moved_in_body_then_used_after.jet:15:17
    |
 15 |     child: task &&owned {
    |                 ^^^^^^^ `owned` moved to a lambda that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `owned` after the move, or give a lambda that captures it a copy with `owned.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
